From 1b859c622458e19cdd235f1e5fa36d79cae71733 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:07:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-0141: NT36672A touch on BLSP1 QUP1 (polled QUP v2
 I2C)

bsd/dev/sweet_nvt.c reads ADT /sweet-touch: votes the BLSP1 AHB clock,
runs the QUP1 I2C core clock from XO, muxes GPIO 2/3 to blsp_i2c1, drives
the touch reset (GPIO 66) high and reads the Novatek parameters at 0x78
(chip id 8). The QUP runs in FIFO mode with v2 tags, polled, one tag stream
per transfer. Touch records (6 bytes at 0x00) are polled at 100 Hz, one
record while idle and all while a finger is down, and go to SweetHID.
sweettouch=0 disables it. SweetHIDTouch takes the panel size from the boot
console instead of topaz's 1080x2400.
---
